+++ b/docs/fixed-page-export.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Fixed-page book exports
+
+Ink Away exports fixed-page books through KOReader's document renderer. PDF,
+CBZ, CBR and other paged sources share the same full-page raster export to PDF
+or PNG. EPUB/MOBI keep their existing reader-layout export. No viewer-specific
+export interface or plugin identifiers are involved.
+
+The saved ink is positioned in native page coordinates. Export uses the original
+pages, regardless of panel zoom, crop, reading direction or a joined fold in the
+viewer. A double-page source image remains one source page. Page ranges and
+With ink select original document pages, not individual panels.
+
+Editable export copies and annotates an actual PDF. The source must have a PDF
+signature; MuPDF's `is_pdf` provider flag alone is insufficient because the same
+provider opens comic archives. This check also guards the editable writer itself.
+The MuPDF annotation-writing capability check is still required for actual PDFs.
+Comic export initially flattens the ink into page images; it does not claim
+editable PDF annotations or rewrite the original archive.
+
+## Quality and resource usage
+
+The export sheet offers Page quality for raster exports of fixed-page books:
+
+| Choice | Long-edge limit | Pixel-count limit | PDF JPEG quality |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Compact (default) | 1600 px | 2 million | 80 |
+| Detailed | 2400 px | 4 million | 90 |
+
+Aspect ratio and native PDF page boxes are retained. Raster size is independent
+of the editor canvas. PNG is lossless at the selected raster size. A low-resolution
+source cannot acquire extra detail through the Detailed setting.
+
+The existing exporter processes one selected page per progress step, streams its
+temporary JPEG into the PDF, deletes the temporary file and collects raster
+buffers before the next step. The source document is released on completion,
+cancellation or failure. Open/render/dimension errors fail the export rather
+than substituting a blank page. Whole archives are not extracted up front.
+Decoded source pages and the host's document caches can still use memory in
+addition to the capped output raster; input archive size alone does not determine
+peak memory. Device refresh, IO and UI scheduling also affect elapsed time.
+
+Direct embedding of original JPEG data and editable annotations over converted
+comic pages remain possible future optimizations, not implemented behavior.
+
+## Verification
+
+`luajit tests/bookexport.lua` exercises actual export specifications with a
+stand-in host: format routing, quality independent of editor size, native
+anchors and widths, mixed dimensions, range/ink-only selection, cleanup and
+render/dimension/open errors. `tests/annots.lua` retains PDF/annotation checks.
+
+`tests/realbb/comic_fixtures.py` generates original synthetic PNG pages in CBZ
+and stored RAR5/CBR archives. It follows the public RAR format description at
+https://www.rarlab.com/technote.htm; no external comic content is downloaded.
+
+From a built KOReader runtime, run:
+
+```
+./luajit REPO/tests/realbb/comicexport.lua REPO
+```
+
+It generates and removes small fixtures automatically. It exercises the real
+MuPDF archive decoder/page renderer, blitbuffers, ink compositor, JPEG encoder
+and PDF writer, with adapted UI/document registry. It reopens the PDF and checks
+page count, dimensions and ink pixels, plus cancellation, scratch cleanup and
+document lifetime. It is registered with the native test runner.
+
+For a larger desktop measurement:
+
+```
+python3 REPO/tests/realbb/comic_fixtures.py /tmp/inkaway-comics --large
+./luajit REPO/tests/realbb/comicexport.lua REPO /tmp/inkaway-comics
+```
+
+This leaves the generated files for inspection and reports CPU time, output size
+and sampled resident memory (including native allocations). The synthetic large
+archives contain 100 noise pages and are approximately 144 MB each. They are not
+a benchmark of reader hardware, compressed/solid RAR archives or unusually large
+individual scanned pages. Live export from the reader toolbar remains necessary.
